# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ForgeMind mobile — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for machine-specific values:
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` and `.env` are gitignored. Only `.env.example` is committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base URL of the ForgeMind backend (forgemind-backend).
#
# You normally do NOT need to change this. `src/config/api.ts` reads this value,
# and if it is left as a loopback address (localhost / 127.0.0.1) the app
# ignores it on a physical device and derives the correct address from Metro
# automatically. That is deliberate: `localhost` on a phone means the phone
# itself, which is the single most common cause of
# "java.net.ConnectException: Failed to connect to localhost/127.0.0.1:3000".
#
# Set this ONLY when you want to pin an address, e.g. to point the phone at a
# backend on a different machine:
#   - Physical device    -> http://<your-LAN-IP>:3000   (backend must bind 0.0.0.0)
#   - Android emulator   -> http://10.0.2.2:3000
#   - iOS simulator / web-> http://localhost:3000
#
# This value is inlined into the app bundle at BUILD time and is NOT a secret.
# After editing it you MUST restart Metro with the cache cleared or the old
# value stays in the bundle:
#     npx expo start -c
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000
